WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.201
-Can I just say hello

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.836
to Carol Burnett's grandmother?
-Yeah, thank you so much.

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:05.671
She really likes that.

00:00:05.671 --> 00:00:08.007
So, this is
a very funny special.

00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:09.242
-Thank you.
-But it's also --

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:12.912
It is about your depression,
your anxiety.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.047
It's very honest.
-Yes.

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:18.051
-When did you realize you wanted
to do an hour about this,

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:19.685
and was that
a hard decision to make?

00:00:19.685 --> 00:00:21.887
-Well, it was
not a hard decision.

00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:23.055
It was out of necessity.

00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:25.258
When I first
started coming back to stand-up,

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:29.029
I was so anxious and sad,
and it was so clear.

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:30.663
Everything about me,
my hands shook.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:32.798
I would bite my lip
until it bled.

00:00:32.798 --> 00:00:35.835
And my hair was wild.
I hadn't shaved.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:38.404
And it was clear something
was off, so I had to address it.

00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:40.740
And the best way,
the safest way,

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.708
with my personality
was to make jokes about it.

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:45.644
So, it was -- it was sort of --

00:00:45.644 --> 00:00:47.546
I feel like it was blessed
from the beginning,

00:00:47.546 --> 00:00:48.715
to be honest with you.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:51.784
-And you brought people
into this special.

00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:53.819
Obviously, most of it is
you on stage,

00:00:53.819 --> 00:00:56.689
but you have conversations
with your mom.

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:58.858
Did she jump at the opportunity
to be in this?

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.661
Did she have hesitation?
-She was dreading it

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:04.297
and spent weeks
scouring the house for --

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:06.599
It was like
she was preparing for Passover.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:07.800
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.168
Which is a big thing for Jews.

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:11.137
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.373
And then she kept asking

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:15.274
if Judd Apatow
could make her look thinner.

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:16.609
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:17.977
She thought
it was an important element

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.278
of your stand-up special.
Sure.

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:21.347
-Yes. Yes.
So, that was a thing,

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:24.150
but I thought she came off,
like, the perfect mom.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.918
Like, if you were to cast a mom,
she was the perfect --

00:01:25.918 --> 00:01:28.721
-Yes. I think she's gonna get
mom parts off of this special.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.156
[ Laughter ]
-I hope so.

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:31.757
-But you -- this was serious.

00:01:31.757 --> 00:01:33.626
You actually considered
retiring from stand-up

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:36.129
based on how bad this depression
was, this anxiety was.

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:38.264
-Yeah.
I had retired from life.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.433
And then I was retiring
from stand-up.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:42.601
And then I thought about it,
and it sounded so pretentious

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:46.239
that -- Carson retired,
and Michael Jordan retired.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.408
-Yeah.
-Gary Gulman, I was giving up.

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:50.243
-Sure.
-I was throwing in the towel.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.111
Yes.
-It's nice that you didn't.

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:53.245
I mentioned your mom.

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:55.715
Also, your wife,
who it's her birthday today.

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:59.519
-Yes, yes.
Happy birthday, Sade.

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:01.287
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:04.690
-And your therapist
is also in the special.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:07.059
Again, were they --

00:02:07.059 --> 00:02:08.761
Was that important to you
to have them in there?

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:11.364
And did they have any hesitation
to participating?

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:15.301
-No, my psychiatrist,
Dr. Richard Friedman,

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:19.839
is incredibly telegenic
and very comfortable on camera,

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:21.107
so it worked out perfectly.

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:24.276
And he didn't hesitate,
and I was excited,

00:02:24.276 --> 00:02:26.846
because his co-pay is very high.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.282
-Yeah.
-So I got a free session.

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:32.217
-[ Laughs ]
-And I thought it was important

00:02:32.217 --> 00:02:36.756
that people saw that it was not
a solo act, recovering from...

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:38.758
-Sure.
-...from a mental illness.

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.159
That my wife was very helpful,

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:42.227
went to every single one
of my appointments.

00:02:42.227 --> 00:02:46.966
And that Dr. Friedman was also
a very valuable component

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.301
in my recovery,
as far as guiding me

00:02:49.301 --> 00:02:52.171
through medication and treatment
and a hospitalization,

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.707
which I had been terrified

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:56.909
by "One Flew Over
the Cuckoo's Nest"

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:58.811
and "Girl, Interrupted"

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.946
and that season
of "American Horror Story."

00:03:00.946 --> 00:03:02.215
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, there's not --

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:04.284
There's not a lot of good movies

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:05.718
about how great a time
that'll be, yeah.

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:07.119
-And I feel like animation

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:08.253
really hasn't
done it justice, either.

00:03:08.253 --> 00:03:11.123
-No.
-So I was terrified.

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:13.860
And he guided me through it
and prepared me,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:18.231
and it turned out to be very
ordinary and so helpful.

